var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-overview","page":"Overview","text":"This package is currently structured around three modules:\n\nGBGPeriodicFields: the top-level module and public re-export surface.\nFields: grids, Cartesian fiber types, field representations, FFT transforms, field utilities, and broadcasting support.\nFieldAlgebra: fiberwise algebraic operations on scalar, vector, and tensor fields.\n\nPages = [\n  \"api/GBGPeriodicFields.md\",\n  \"api/Fields.md\",\n  \"api/FieldAlgebra.md\",\n]\nDepth = 2","title":"API overview"},{"category":"section","location":"api/GBGPeriodicFields/#GBGPeriodicFields.jl","page":"GBGPeriodicFields","text":"","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"api/GBGPeriodicFields/#Re-exported-modules","page":"GBGPeriodicFields","text":"The top-level module includes and re-exports the public interface of:\n\nGBGPeriodicFields.Fields\nGBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra","title":"Re-exported modules"},{"category":"module","location":"api/GBGPeriodicFields/#GBGPeriodicFields.GBGPeriodicFields","page":"GBGPeriodicFields","text":"GBGPeriodicFields\n\nTools for representing, transforming, and manipulating scalar, vector, and tensor fields on three-dimensional rectangular periodic domains.\n\nThe package is aimed primarily at fluid-dynamics and turbulence simulations, with physical-space and real-to-complex spectral representations designed for both CPU and GPU array backends. It also targets Lagrangian particle simulations through interpolation tools for evaluating fields between grid nodes.\n\nThe package provides field representations, FFT transform plans, storage-wise broadcasting, and algebraic operations on fields.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.GBGPeriodicFields"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#FieldAlgebra.jl","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"Pages = [\"FieldAlgebra.md\"]","title":"FieldAlgebra.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Field-vector-space-operations","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"The allocating forms are provided by methods of Base.+ and Base.- for compatible field and constant-fiber combinations.","title":"Field vector-space operations"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Multiplication-and-division","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"The allocating forms are provided by methods of Base.* and Base./ where the corresponding operation is representation-wise meaningful.","title":"Multiplication and division"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Vector-products","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"The allocating forms are provided by methods of LinearAlgebra.dot and LinearAlgebra.cross. The infix Unicode aliases ⋅ and × are also exported.","title":"Vector products"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Tensor-vector-and-tensor-tensor-products","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"The allocating tensor-vector and tensor-tensor forms are provided by methods of Base.*.","title":"Tensor-vector and tensor-tensor products"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Tensor-index-permutations","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"The allocating tensor-index transpose is provided by methods of Base.transpose.","title":"Tensor index permutations"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Tensor-contractions-and-field-norms","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"Fiberwise vector inner products and tensor Frobenius inner products are provided by methods of LinearAlgebra.dot and documented together with dot!.","title":"Tensor contractions and field norms"},{"category":"section","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#Tensor-decompositions","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"","title":"Tensor decompositions"},{"category":"module","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"FieldAlgebra\n\nFiberwise algebraic operations on fields in physical-space and spectral representations.\n\nThis module provides local algebra on scalar, vector, and tensor fibers. The operations act on the physical field represented by the data, not on the storage representation as an object of interest.\n\nProvided operations include:\n\nfield vector-space operations: +, -, add!, subtract!;\nmultiplication and division by real numbers: *, /, multiply!, divide!;\nscalar-field multiplication and division where representation-wise meaningful;\nconstant additions to scalar, vector, and second-order tensor fields;\nvector operations: dot, ⋅, cross, ×, dot!, cross!;\nsecond-order tensor operations: mul!, *, transpose, transpose!, sym, skew, dev, norm;\ntensor contractions: Frobenius inner products through dot and dot!.\n\nRepresentation rules:\n\noperations in physical-space representation are pointwise;\nlinear operations are also defined in spectral representation when they can be applied coefficient-wise;\nconstant additions in spectral representation update only the zero Fourier mode;\nnonlinear products, divisions, and norms are restricted to physical-space representation unless one non-scalar factor is a constant fiber object.\n\nGlobal products, global norms, integration-based adjoints, and differential operators are intentionally outside this module.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.add!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"add!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  a::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  b::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  fields::AbstractFieldPhysical...,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  a::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  b::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  fields::AbstractFieldSpectral...,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  scalar::Real,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  field::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  scalar::Real,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  field::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  field::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  field::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nadd!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  field::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nAdd fields or constants in-place.\n\nField-field addition is storage-wise and representation-preserving: pointwise for fields in physical-space representation and coefficientwise for fields in spectral representation.\n\nAdding a real number is defined for scalar fields. In physical-space representation it adds the number to all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient.\n\nAdding a constant fiber vector is defined for vector fields. In physical-space representation it adds the vector to all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient of each vector component.\n\nAdding a constant second-order fiber tensor is defined for second-order tensor fields. In physical-space representation it adds the tensor to all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient of each tensor component.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.add!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.subtract!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"subtract!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  a::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  b::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  fields::AbstractFieldPhysical...,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  a::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  b::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  fields::AbstractFieldSpectral...,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  scalar::Real,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  field::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  scalar::Real,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  field::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  field::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  field::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nsubtract!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  field::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nSubtract fields or constants in-place.\n\nField-field subtraction is storage-wise and representation-preserving, computing a - b - fields....\n\nSubtracting a real number is defined for scalar fields. In physical-space representation it subtracts the number from all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient.\n\nSubtracting a constant fiber vector is defined for vector fields. In physical-space representation it subtracts the vector from all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient of each vector component.\n\nSubtracting a constant second-order fiber tensor is defined for second-order tensor fields. In physical-space representation it subtracts the tensor from all grid-point values. In spectral representation it modifies only the zero Fourier coefficient of each tensor component.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.subtract!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.multiply!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"multiply!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  field::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n)\n\nmultiply!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  field::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\nmultiply!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nmultiply!(\n  destination::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\nmultiply!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nmultiply!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nMultiply by a scalar field in-place.\n\nMultiplication by a scalar field in physical-space representation is pointwise and acts on all tensor components of the field.\n\nMultiplication of a scalar field by a constant fiber vector or a constant second-order fiber tensor is defined in both representations. In physical-space representation it is pointwise. In spectral representation it is coefficient-wise, because the operation is linear in the scalar field.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.multiply!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.divide!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"divide!(\n  destination::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  field::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ndivide!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  scalar::Real,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ndivide!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ndivide!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\nDivide a field, a real number, or a constant fiber object in-place by a compatible scalar field in physical-space representation.\n\nDivision by a scalar field in physical-space representation is pointwise. When the numerator is a field, the division acts on all tensor components of that field. When the numerator is a real number, the result is a scalar field in physical-space representation. When the numerator is a constant fiber vector or second-order fiber tensor, the result is the corresponding vector or tensor field in physical-space representation.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.divide!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dot!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"dot!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  B::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\ndot!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  B::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\ndot!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n  B::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\ndot!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  B::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\ndot!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldSpectral,\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n  B::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nCompute the fiberwise Frobenius inner product of second-order tensors in-place.\n\nThis computes the double contraction Aᵢⱼ * Bᵢⱼ.\n\nFor two tensor fields this is defined only in physical-space representation. Methods for spectral representation are defined only when one factor is a constant fiber tensor, so the operation remains coefficient-wise.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dot!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.cross!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"cross!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  u::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  v::VectorFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ncross!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  u::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\ncross!(\n  destination::VectorFieldPhysical,\n  a::FiberVector,\n  u::VectorFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ncross!(\n  destination::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  u::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  a::FiberVector,\n)\n\ncross!(\n  destination::VectorFieldSpectral,\n  a::FiberVector,\n  u::VectorFieldSpectral,\n)\n\nCompute a fiberwise cross product in-place.\n\nFor two vector fields this is defined only in physical-space representation and computes u × v pointwise.\n\nFor a vector field and a constant fiber vector this computes the corresponding fiberwise cross product. The methods for spectral representation are defined only for cross products with a constant fiber vector.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.cross!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#LinearAlgebra.mul!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"mul!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  B::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\nmul!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  B::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nmul!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n  B::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\nmul!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  B::FiberTensor2,\n)\n\nmul!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::FiberTensor2,\n  B::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nCompute the fiberwise product of second-order tensors in-place.\n\nThis computes (A * B)ᵢⱼ = Aᵢₖ * Bₖⱼ.\n\nFor two tensor fields this is defined only in physical-space representation. Methods for spectral representation are defined only when one factor is a constant fiber tensor, so the operation remains coefficient-wise.\n\nThe five-argument form computes destination = α * product + β * destination.\n\nAs for LinearAlgebra.mul!, destination must not share storage with either input.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LinearAlgebra.mul!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#LinearAlgebra.transpose!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"transpose!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\ntranspose!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nTranspose the fiber indices of a second-order tensor field in-place.\n\nThis computes destinationᵢⱼ = Aⱼᵢ, leaving the physical-space or spectral-space representation unchanged. The operation is linear, so it is defined for both representations.\n\nUnlike Julia's matrix transpose, this method writes a canonical tensor-field representation, not a lazy transpose wrapper.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LinearAlgebra.transpose!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.norm!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"norm!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n)\n\nnorm!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  u::VectorFieldPhysical,\n)\n\nnorm!(\n  destination::ScalarFieldPhysical,\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\nCompute the fiberwise norm of a field in physical-space representation in-place.\n\nFor scalar fields this computes the pointwise absolute value abs(φ).\n\nFor vector fields this computes the Euclidean norm sqrt(uᵢ * uᵢ).\n\nFor second-order tensor fields this computes the Frobenius norm sqrt(Aᵢⱼ * Aᵢⱼ), not the operator norm.\n\nThis is a pointwise physical-space operation and is not defined for spectral representation.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.norm!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#LinearAlgebra.norm","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"norm(scalar_field::ScalarFieldPhysical)\n\nnorm(u::VectorFieldPhysical)\n\nnorm(A::TensorFieldPhysical{2})\n\nAllocate and compute the fiberwise norm of a field in physical-space representation.\n\nFor scalar fields this returns the scalar field abs(φ).\n\nFor vector fields this returns the scalar field sqrt(uᵢ * uᵢ).\n\nFor second-order tensor fields this returns the Frobenius norm field sqrt(Aᵢⱼ * Aᵢⱼ), not the operator norm. Use dot(u, u) or dot(A, A) for the corresponding squared norms.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"LinearAlgebra.norm"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.sym!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"sym!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\nsym!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nCompute the symmetric part of a second-order tensor field in-place.\n\nThis computes sym(A) = (A + transpose(A)) / 2.\n\nThe operation is linear and representation-preserving, so it is defined for tensor fields in physical-space and spectral representations.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.sym!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.sym","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"sym(A::TensorFieldPhysical{2})\n\nsym(A::TensorFieldSpectral{2})\n\nsym(A::FiberTensor2)\n\nAllocate and compute the symmetric part of a second-order tensor.\n\nFor tensor fields this is a fiberwise operation. For a constant fiber tensor this returns a constant fiber tensor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.sym"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.skew!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"skew!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\nskew!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nCompute the skew-symmetric part of a second-order tensor field in-place.\n\nThis computes skew(A) = (A - transpose(A)) / 2.\n\nThe operation is linear and representation-preserving, so it is defined for tensor fields in physical-space and spectral representations.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.skew!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.skew","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"skew(A::TensorFieldPhysical{2})\n\nskew(A::TensorFieldSpectral{2})\n\nskew(A::FiberTensor2)\n\nAllocate and compute the skew-symmetric part of a second-order tensor.\n\nFor tensor fields this is a fiberwise operation. For a constant fiber tensor this returns a constant fiber tensor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.skew"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dev!","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"dev!(\n  destination::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n  A::TensorFieldPhysical{2},\n)\n\ndev!(\n  destination::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n  A::TensorFieldSpectral{2},\n)\n\nCompute the deviatoric part of a second-order tensor field in-place.\n\nThis computes dev(A) = A - tr(A) * I / 3.\n\nThe operation is linear and representation-preserving, so it is defined for tensor fields in physical-space and spectral representations.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dev!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/FieldAlgebra/#GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dev","page":"FieldAlgebra.jl","text":"dev(A::TensorFieldPhysical{2})\n\ndev(A::TensorFieldSpectral{2})\n\ndev(A::FiberTensor2)\n\nAllocate and compute the deviatoric part of a second-order tensor.\n\nFor tensor fields this is a fiberwise operation. For a constant fiber tensor this returns a constant fiber tensor.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.FieldAlgebra.dev"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Fields.jl","page":"Fields","text":"Pages = [\"Fields.md\"]","title":"Fields.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Fixed-fiber-types","page":"Fields","text":"","title":"Fixed fiber types"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Domain-and-Fourier-layout","page":"Fields","text":"","title":"Domain and Fourier layout"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Abstract-field-interface","page":"Fields","text":"","title":"Abstract field interface"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Field-types","page":"Fields","text":"","title":"Field types"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Field-utilities","page":"Fields","text":"These functions allocate fields with compatible metadata or check whether fields are compatible for representation-preserving operations. They are used internally by the field algebra and are documented here because they are part of the field infrastructure.","title":"Field utilities"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Transforming-between-representations","page":"Fields","text":"","title":"Transforming between representations"},{"category":"section","location":"api/Fields/#Broadcasting","page":"Fields","text":"Field broadcasting is storage-wise and representation-preserving. Dotted assignments write into the destination field storage, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions allocate a compatible field in the same representation.","title":"Broadcasting"},{"category":"module","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields","page":"Fields","text":"Fields\n\nField representation and transform core for scalar, vector, and tensor fields on three-dimensional rectangular periodic domains.\n\nThis module defines grids, Cartesian fiber types, Fourier-layout conventions, field types for physical-space representation and real-to-complex spectral representation, FFT transform plans, and storage-wise broadcasting designed for CPU and GPU array backends.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberVector","page":"Fields","text":"FiberVector{T}\n\nStatic three-component Cartesian vector type used for individual vector values.\n\nThis is an alias for SVector{3, T}, with scalar type T.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberVector"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor2","page":"Fields","text":"FiberTensor2{T}\n\nStatic second-order Cartesian tensor type used for individual tensor values.\n\nThis is an alias for SMatrix{3, 3, T, 9}, with scalar type T.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor2"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor3","page":"Fields","text":"FiberTensor3{T}\n\nStatic third-order Cartesian tensor type used for individual tensor values.\n\nThis is an alias for SArray{Tuple{3, 3, 3}, T, 3, 27}, with scalar type T.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor3"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor4","page":"Fields","text":"FiberTensor4{T}\n\nStatic fourth-order Cartesian tensor type used for individual tensor values.\n\nThis is an alias for SArray{Tuple{3, 3, 3, 3}, T, 4, 81}, with scalar type T.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FiberTensor4"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.Grid3D","page":"Fields","text":"Grid3D(\n  grid_size::NTuple{3, Int},\n  domain_size::NTuple{3, T},\n  grid_spacing::NTuple{3, T},\n  origin::NTuple{3, T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nGrid3D(\n  grid_size::NTuple{3, Int},\n  domain_size::NTuple{3, T};\n  origin::NTuple{3, T} = (zero(T), zero(T), zero(T)),\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nUniform three-dimensional grid for a periodic rectangular domain.\n\nThe fields are\n\ngrid_size::NTuple{3, Int}: the number of grid points in each spatial direction.\ndomain_size::NTuple{3, T}: the length of the domain in each spatial direction.\ngrid_spacing::NTuple{3, T}: the spacing between adjacent grid points in each spatial direction.\norigin::NTuple{3, T}: the physical coordinates of the first grid point.\n\nThe two-argument constructor computes grid_spacing = domain_size ./ grid_size.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.Grid3D"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.RealFourierLayout","page":"Fields","text":"RealFourierLayout()\nRealFourierLayout(fft_dims::NTuple{3, Int})\n\nLayout convention for three-dimensional real-to-complex Fourier transforms.\n\nHere fft_dims is the tuple of transformed dimensions passed to the FFT planner. The main role of the ordering is to specify the real-FFT half dimension: in dimension fft_dims[1], only the nonnegative frequencies are represented, while the other dimensions use the full complex FFT frequency ordering.\n\nThe zero-argument constructor uses fft_dims = (1, 2, 3).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.RealFourierLayout"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.validate_fft_dims","page":"Fields","text":"validate_fft_dims(d::NTuple{3, Int})\n\nCheck whether d is a valid ordering of the three spatial Fourier-transform dimensions. Returns true or false.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.validate_fft_dims"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.rfft_shape","page":"Fields","text":"rfft_shape(grid_size::NTuple{3, Int}, fft_dims::NTuple{3, Int})\n\nReturn the shape of the nonredundant real-to-complex Fourier representation of a three-dimensional real field.\n\nHere grid_size is the physical grid size and fft_dims is the order of transformed dimensions. The dimension fft_dims[1] is the real-FFT half dimension: it is stored with length grid_size[fft_dims[1]] ÷ 2 + 1, while the other dimensions keep their physical-grid lengths.\n\nReturns a three-tuple giving the spectral array size.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.rfft_shape"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.AbstractFieldPhysical","page":"Fields","text":"AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R}\n\nAbstract supertype for fields represented by values in physical space.\n\nHere T<:AbstractFloat is the real scalar type associated with the field and R is the tensor order stored as an integer value parameter. Concrete subtypes provide the actual storage and metadata. The generic field interface obtains T and R through field_scalar_type and field_tensor_order, and obtains the stored data through field_data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.AbstractFieldPhysical"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.AbstractFieldSpectral","page":"Fields","text":"AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R}\n\nAbstract supertype for fields represented by Fourier coefficients in spectral space.\n\nHere T<:AbstractFloat is the real scalar type associated with the field and R is the tensor order stored as an integer value parameter. Concrete subtypes provide the actual storage and metadata. The generic field interface obtains T and R through field_scalar_type and field_tensor_order, and obtains the stored data through field_data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.AbstractFieldSpectral"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_data","page":"Fields","text":"field_data(field::AbstractField)\n\nReturn the array storing the field data.\n\nFor fields represented in physical space, this is the array of values on the grid. For fields represented in spectral space, this is the array of Fourier coefficients.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_data"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_grid","page":"Fields","text":"field_grid(field::AbstractField)\n\nReturn the Grid3D associated with a field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_grid"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_layout","page":"Fields","text":"field_layout(field::AbstractField)\n\nReturn the RealFourierLayout associated with a field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_layout"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_scalar_type","page":"Fields","text":"field_scalar_type(\n  field::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nfield_scalar_type(\n  field::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nReturn the real scalar type T associated with a field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_scalar_type"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_tensor_order","page":"Fields","text":"field_tensor_order(\n  field::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nfield_tensor_order(\n  field::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nReturn the tensor order R of a field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.field_tensor_order"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.fiber_shape","page":"Fields","text":"fiber_shape(::Val{R}) where {R}\n\nReturn the tensor-fiber shape associated with tensor order R.\n\nFor scalar fields, R = 0 gives (). For higher tensor orders, each tensor index has length 3, so R = 1 gives (3,), R = 2 gives (3, 3), and so on.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.fiber_shape"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.physical_field_shape","page":"Fields","text":"physical_field_shape(grid::Grid3D, ::Val{R}) where {R}\n\nReturn the storage shape of a field of tensor order R represented in physical space on grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.physical_field_shape"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.spectral_field_shape","page":"Fields","text":"spectral_field_shape(\n  grid::Grid3D,\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n  ::Val{R},\n) where {R}\n\nReturn the storage shape of a field of tensor order R represented in nonredundant real-to-complex spectral space.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.spectral_field_shape"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.ScalarFieldPhysical","page":"Fields","text":"ScalarFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, 3},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nScalarFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, 3},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nScalar field in physical-space representation, stored as its values on a three-dimensional physical grid.\n\nHere values_at_grid contains the real scalar values, grid is the Grid3D on which the values are sampled, and fourier_layout is the RealFourierLayout used when transforming the field.\n\nBroadcasting over scalar fields in physical-space representation is lifted to values_at_grid. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.values_at_grid, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new ScalarFieldPhysical.\n\nThe two-argument constructor uses the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.ScalarFieldPhysical"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.ScalarFieldSpectral","page":"Fields","text":"ScalarFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, 3},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nScalarFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, 3},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nScalar field in spectral representation, stored as its nonredundant real-to-complex Fourier coefficients.\n\nHere fourier_coefficients contains the complex Fourier coefficients in real-FFT storage, grid is the Grid3D associated with the physical domain, and fourier_layout is the RealFourierLayout specifying the transformed dimensions and the real-FFT half dimension.\n\nThe coefficient array has shape spectral_field_shape(grid, fourier_layout, Val(0)). The dimension fourier_layout.fft_dims[1] is the real-FFT half dimension.\n\nBroadcasting over scalar fields in spectral representation is lifted to fourier_coefficients. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.fourier_coefficients, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new ScalarFieldSpectral. All such operations are coefficientwise; for example, .* does not represent a pseudospectral product of scalar fields.\n\nThe two-argument constructor uses the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.ScalarFieldSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.VectorFieldPhysical","page":"Fields","text":"VectorFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, 4},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nVectorFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, 4},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nVector field in physical-space representation, stored as its components on a three-dimensional physical grid.\n\nHere values_at_grid contains the real vector components with storage order values_at_grid[i, j, k, α], where α = 1, 2, 3, grid is the Grid3D on which the values are sampled, and fourier_layout is the RealFourierLayout used when transforming the field.\n\nBroadcasting over vector fields in physical-space representation is lifted to values_at_grid. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.values_at_grid, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new VectorFieldPhysical. These operations are storage-wise and componentwise.\n\nThe two-argument constructor uses the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.VectorFieldPhysical"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.VectorFieldSpectral","page":"Fields","text":"VectorFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, 4},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nVectorFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, 4},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nVector field in spectral representation, stored as its nonredundant real-to-complex Fourier coefficients.\n\nHere fourier_coefficients contains the complex vector Fourier coefficients in real-FFT storage, with the component index last: fourier_coefficients[i, j, k, α], where α = 1, 2, 3. The spatial part has shape spectral_field_shape(grid, fourier_layout, Val(0)), and the full array has shape spectral_field_shape(grid, fourier_layout, Val(1)). The dimension fourier_layout.fft_dims[1] is the real-FFT half dimension.\n\nBroadcasting over vector fields in spectral representation is lifted to fourier_coefficients. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.fourier_coefficients, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new VectorFieldSpectral. These operations are storage-wise and componentwise. They do not represent pseudospectral products or tensor contractions.\n\nThe two-argument constructor uses the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.VectorFieldSpectral"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.TensorFieldPhysical","page":"Fields","text":"TensorFieldPhysical{R}(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {R, T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nTensorFieldPhysical{R}(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {R, T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nTensorFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, N},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, N}\n\nTensorFieldPhysical(\n  values_at_grid::AbstractArray{T, N},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, N}\n\nTensor field of order R ≥ 2 in physical-space representation, stored as its components on a three-dimensional physical grid.\n\nHere values_at_grid contains the real tensor components with storage order values_at_grid[i, j, k, α₁, ..., αᵣ], where each tensor index has length 3, grid is the Grid3D on which the values are sampled, and fourier_layout is the RealFourierLayout used when transforming the field.\n\nThe array has shape physical_field_shape(grid, Val(R)). The constructors without explicit {R} infer R = N - 3 from the array dimension N.\n\nBroadcasting over tensor fields in physical-space representation is lifted to values_at_grid. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.values_at_grid, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new TensorFieldPhysical. These operations are storage-wise and componentwise. They do not represent tensor contractions.\n\nThe two-argument constructors use the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.TensorFieldPhysical"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.TensorFieldSpectral","page":"Fields","text":"TensorFieldSpectral{R}(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {R, T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nTensorFieldSpectral{R}(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {R, T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nTensorFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, N},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n  fourier_layout::RealFourierLayout,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, N}\n\nTensorFieldSpectral(\n  fourier_coefficients::AbstractArray{Complex{T}, N},\n  grid::Grid3D{T},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, N}\n\nTensor field of order R ≥ 2 in spectral representation, stored as its nonredundant real-to-complex Fourier coefficients.\n\nHere fourier_coefficients contains the complex tensor Fourier coefficients in real-FFT storage, with the tensor indices last: fourier_coefficients[i, j, k, α₁, ..., αᵣ], where each tensor index has length 3. The spatial part has shape spectral_field_shape(grid, fourier_layout, Val(0)), and the full array has shape spectral_field_shape(grid, fourier_layout, Val(R)). The dimension fourier_layout.fft_dims[1] is the real-FFT half dimension.\n\nBroadcasting over tensor fields in spectral representation is lifted to fourier_coefficients. Thus dotted assignments such as @. destination = a - b + c write into destination.fourier_coefficients, while field-valued out-of-place dotted expressions return a new TensorFieldSpectral. These operations are storage-wise and componentwise. They do not represent pseudospectral products or tensor contractions.\n\nThe two-argument constructors use the default RealFourierLayout() for the layout.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.TensorFieldSpectral"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_field","page":"Fields","text":"similar_field(reference::AbstractField, data)\n\nsimilar_field(reference::AbstractField, ::Val{R})\n\nConstruct a field with metadata copied from reference.\n\nWith storage array data, the field has the same representation and tensor order as reference. With Val{R}, new storage is allocated with the same representation and tensor order R.\n\nThis is used by out-of-place field broadcasting and by allocating algebraic operations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_field"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_physical_field","page":"Fields","text":"similar_physical_field(reference::AbstractFieldSpectral, data)\n\nConstruct a field represented in physical space with storage array data and metadata copied from the spectral-space reference.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_physical_field"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_spectral_field","page":"Fields","text":"similar_spectral_field(reference::AbstractFieldPhysical, data)\n\nConstruct a field represented in spectral space with storage array data and metadata copied from the physical-space reference.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.similar_spectral_field"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.check_field_compatibility","page":"Fields","text":"check_field_compatibility(\n  a::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n  b::AbstractFieldPhysical,\n)\n\ncheck_field_compatibility(\n  a::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n  b::AbstractFieldSpectral,\n)\n\nCheck that two fields with the same representation have the same scalar type, tensor order, grid, and Fourier layout.\n\nReturns nothing or throws an exception.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.check_field_compatibility"},{"category":"type","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FieldTransforms","page":"Fields","text":"FieldTransforms(\n  physical::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n  spectral::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R};\n  fft_flags = nothing,\n  fft_timelimit = Inf,\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nForward and inverse FFT plans connecting compatible fields represented in physical and spectral space.\n\nHere physical provides the real-space storage array, spectral provides the real-to-complex Fourier coefficient array, fft_flags is an optional backend-specific FFT planner flag, and fft_timelimit is the planner time limit used when fft_flags is provided. Only the spatial dimensions field_layout(physical).fft_dims are transformed; tensor-fiber dimensions are left untransformed.\n\nThe fields are\n\ngrid::G: the Grid3D for which the plans were constructed.\nfourier_layout::L: the RealFourierLayout for which the plans were constructed.\nplan_forward_fft::PF: the plan transforming physical values to spectral coefficients.\nplan_inverse_fft::PI: the plan transforming spectral coefficients to physical values.\n\nThe plans are backend-, array-type-, scalar-type-, and tensor-order-specific; construct a separate FieldTransforms object for each CPU/GPU backend and field tensor order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.FieldTransforms"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_physical!","page":"Fields","text":"to_physical!(\n  physical::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n  spectral::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R},\n  transforms::FieldTransforms{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nTransform a field from spectral space to physical space in-place.\n\nHere physical is the destination, spectral is the source, and transforms provides the inverse FFT plan.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_physical!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_spectral!","page":"Fields","text":"to_spectral!(\n  spectral::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R},\n  physical::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n  transforms::FieldTransforms{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nTransform a field from physical space to spectral space in-place.\n\nHere spectral is the destination, physical is the source, and transforms provides the forward FFT plan.\n\nReturns the modified destination field.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_spectral!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_physical","page":"Fields","text":"to_physical(\n  spectral::AbstractFieldSpectral{T, R},\n  transforms::FieldTransforms{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nAllocating version of to_physical!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_physical"},{"category":"function","location":"api/Fields/#GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_spectral","page":"Fields","text":"to_spectral(\n  physical::AbstractFieldPhysical{T, R},\n  transforms::FieldTransforms{T, R},\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat, R}\n\nAllocating version of to_spectral!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.Fields.to_spectral"},{"category":"section","location":"#GBGPeriodicFields.jl","page":"Home","text":"GBGPeriodicFields.jl is a package for representing, transforming, and manipulating scalar, vector, and tensor fields on three-dimensional rectangular periodic domains.\n\nThe package is aimed primarily at fluid-dynamics and turbulence simulations. Fields are physical objects, while physical-space and nonredundant spectral representations are storage and manipulation choices. The implementation is designed for both CPU and GPU array backends, and the package is intended to support later Lagrangian-particle and interpolation tools.\n\nThis package is not intended to be a ready-to-use DNS solver; rather, it is a toolkit for building fluid-dynamics and general field solvers.","title":"GBGPeriodicFields.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"This is an unregistered package, so it is not listed in the General Julia registry. To install it, run:\n\n]add https://github.com/GrigorySarnitsky/GBGPeriodicFields.jl\n\nor\n\nusing Pkg\n\nPkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/GrigorySarnitsky/GBGPeriodicFields.jl\")\n\nThen you can use it as usual:\n\nusing GBGPeriodicFields","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Main-components","page":"Home","text":"Fields: grids, Cartesian fiber types, field representations, FFT transforms, field utilities, and broadcasting support.\nFieldAlgebra: fiberwise algebraic operations on fields, including vector-space operations, scalar actions, vector products, tensor products, tensor contractions, norms, and tensor decompositions.\n\nGlobal products, global norms, integration-based adjoints, and differential operators are intentionally outside the current algebra module.","title":"Main components"},{"category":"section","location":"#Documentation-structure","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Documentation structure"},{"category":"section","location":"#General-documentation","page":"Home","text":"Pages = [\"index.md\"]","title":"General documentation"},{"category":"section","location":"#API-reference","page":"Home","text":"Pages = [\"api.md\", \"api/GBGPeriodicFields.md\", \"api/Fields.md\", \"api/FieldAlgebra.md\"]","title":"API reference"}]
}
